# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Why this file exists: cambrian-core was checked out CRLF (Windows dev,
# core.autocrlf=true) while the sibling repos that vendor its proto — ui/ and
# cli/ — are LF. Every cross-repo diff of operator.proto therefore reported the
# whole file as changed. The real drift at the time was 34 lines; the raw diff
# said 4,788, and that noise is exactly what lets genuine contract drift go
# unnoticed. `gofmt` also treats a CRLF Go file as unformatted, so ~89 files
# reported as needing formatting when none of them did.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the repository AND on checkout, and it
# overrides core.autocrlf, so the tree is identical on every platform.
#
# ─── Adopting this on an existing checkout ───────────────────────────────────
# Adding the file changes nothing on its own. On a CLEAN tree (no uncommitted
# work — this rewrites almost every file), run:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git status          # review: should be line-ending changes only
#     git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings to LF"
#
# Deliberately not done as part of the audit: the working tree carried
# substantial in-flight work, and renormalising would have buried it under an
# ~800-file diff.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary / generated assets git must not touch.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.rar  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.so   binary
*.dylib binary
*.db   binary

# Generated protobuf bindings. Still LF, but marked so they are collapsed in
# diffs and excluded from language statistics — they are output, not source.
*.pb.go      linguist-generated=true
*_grpc.pb.go linguist-generated=true
